docs/infra.md:70:**Teams and People** (`/api/*`, `packages/cloudflare/src/DirectoryHandlers.ts`, rules in `packages/domain/src/people/Directory.ts`, permissions in `Permissions.ts`). The Durable Object authorizes and commits each change in one transaction, then the Worker puts the D1 index and the email queue in step. Removing a Person marks them removed in the Durable Object (the per-request check denies them at once), deletes their `person_index` row, and ends their Memberships, with history kept.
docs/infra.md:100:| `production` | Sends through Cloudflare Email Sending from `team@notify.surveybeat.app` | The `notify.surveybeat.app` sending subdomain, the `send_email` binding, the `EmailEvents` queue, and its event subscription |
docs/infra.md:113:**The `send_email` binding is named `SendEmail`.** Binding names share one namespace per Worker. Until #147 it was named `Email`, like the Email queue's producer binding; the deploy kept only the queue, so production queued each rendered email instead of sending it and every send failed as `unknown`. Read the deployed bindings back with `cf workers versions get <version> --worker-id <main worker>` when email stops arriving.
docs/infra.md:115:**Send states.** `pending → sending → sent | failed(reason)`. A delivery takes a two-minute lease before calling the provider, and the call times out after 30 seconds. A clear rejection (`E_RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED` and other coded errors) returns the send to `pending` and the message is retried after 30 s, 60 s, and 120 s; the fourth rejection fails it. Permanent rejections (`E_RECIPIENT_SUPPRESSED`, sender and header errors) fail at once. An error without a code, a timeout, or a lease that expired with no outcome fails the send as `unknown`, and it is never resent automatically. A message the queue dead-letters fails its send too (`abandoned`, or `rejected` after earlier rejections).
docs/infra.md:117:**Resend.** An Organization admin can resend a failed send from the Failed emails list in Organization settings (`POST /api/organization/failed-emails/:sendId/resend`, #159). The same send goes back to `pending` under its id, with its stored content and recipient, and is queued again; the consumer renders it as on the first delivery. A complained-about send is never resent, and an Invitation, reminder, or test email only while its link is still live (Invitation not revoked or re-sent since, test send still kept). Repeating the request sends it once.

